[comment {-*- tcl -*- doctools manpage}]
[manpage_begin tclutils::tummdb n 0.1]
[moddesc   {tclutils}]
[titledesc {Pure-Tcl reader for the MaxMind DB (.mmdb) binary format}]
[require Tcl 8.6]
[require tclutils::tubin 0.2]
[require tclutils::tummdb 0.1]
[description]

This package reads MaxMind DB ([term .mmdb]) files, version 2.0 of the binary
format, in pure Tcl. It resolves IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to their associated
data records and works with GeoLite2, GeoIP2 and DB-IP style databases.

All binary primitives are taken from [package tclutils::tubin]
([cmd uintbe], [cmd f32be], [cmd f64be], [cmd u8]).

[para]

The file is loaded fully into memory when opened; lookups are then a binary
search over the database's prefix tree followed by decoding the data record.

[section COMMANDS]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [cmd ::tclutils::tummdb::open] [arg path]]

Open the database at [arg path] and return an opaque [arg handle] used by the
other commands. Throws an error (error code [const {TCLUTILS TUMMDB FORMAT}])
if the file is not a valid MaxMind DB.

[call [cmd ::tclutils::tummdb::metadata] [arg handle]]

Return the database metadata as a dictionary. Always present keys include
[const node_count], [const record_size], [const ip_version],
[const database_type] and [const build_epoch].

[call [cmd ::tclutils::tummdb::lookup] [arg handle] [arg ip]]

Look up [arg ip] (an IPv4 or IPv6 address string). Returns the decoded record
as a nested structure (maps become dictionaries, arrays become lists,
localized names appear under a [const names] sub-dictionary), or the empty
string if the address is not contained in the database.

[call [cmd ::tclutils::tummdb::close] [arg handle]]

Release the resources associated with [arg handle].

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require tclutils::tummdb

set h [::tclutils::tummdb::open /path/to/GeoLite2-City.mmdb]
set r [::tclutils::tummdb::lookup $h 81.2.69.142]
puts [dict get $r country iso_code]   ;# GB
puts [dict get $r city names en]      ;# London
::tclutils::tummdb::close $h
}]

[section "ERROR CODES"]

[list_begin definitions]
[def {TCLUTILS TUMMDB FORMAT}]    File is not a valid MaxMind DB.
[def {TCLUTILS TUMMDB HANDLE}]    Unknown handle passed to a command.
[def {TCLUTILS TUMMDB RECORDSIZE}] Unsupported tree record size.
[def {TCLUTILS TUMMDB TYPE}]      Unsupported data type in the record.
[list_end]

[section LIMITATIONS]

The whole database is held in memory while open. The data section is limited
to 4 GB by the format. The interpretation of record fields (which keys exist)
is defined by the database, not by this reader.

[see_also tclutils::tubin]
[keywords mmdb MaxMind GeoIP geolocation IP binary]
[manpage_end]
